# Single source of every pin of the competitor images (read by `smrt-bench docker-check`, which
# passes each entry that a Dockerfile declares as `ARG KEY=...` as a build argument, and by the
# lint, which fails when a Dockerfile's default differs from the value here).
#
# *_DIGEST: index (multi-arch) digests, so one pin serves linux/arm64 and linux/amd64. Read with
# `docker buildx imagetools inspect <image>:<tag>`; the hex part after `sha256:`. UNSET is refused.
# *_COMMIT, *_VERSION: source pins, verified by `git rev-parse` or the driver's --version in the build.
#
# condaforge/miniforge3:24.9.2-0, index digest read on 2026-11-05.
MINIFORGE_DIGEST=937dc1e8ab9ffc5f388f0d2a1ce5d24ba5b15850771571d7442fac1af53f3fad
# ubuntu:24.04, index digest read the same way on the same day.
UBUNTU_DIGEST=fe81560990fae86dc4743202b2cb4d3df98d0bcf949173cecef15ce1127ef852
# double-down (source fallback of dagmc-dd) and DAGMC.
DOUBLE_DOWN_COMMIT=437ad209eac5
DAGMC_VERSION=3.2.4
# XDG (xdg-org/xdg, 2026-11-06 "Switching out tmate session for debugging CI runner to upterm (#266)",
# the upstream HEAD read with `git ls-remote https://github.com/xdg-org/xdg` at W4-RT-XDG; never a
# personal fork, which lags; same sources as 12f56f1, only .github/workflows/ci.yml differs) and
# MOAB: the same MOAB as the conda DAGMC images (5.6.0), so every row is fed by one MOAB. XDG builds
# on x86_64 only (include/xdg/vec3da.h includes <immintrin.h> unconditionally), so on linux/aarch64
# `docker-check` reports the xdg image Failed with the compile error and no xdg row is run.
XDG_COMMIT=a5d67e635b96
MOAB_VERSION=5.6.0
